==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|over-}}, from {{inh|en|ang|ofer-||over-}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*ubar-||over-}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|over-}}, {{cog|de|über-}}, {{cog|da|over-}}, {{cog|sv|över-}}. {{doublet|en|super-|sur-|hyper}}. More at {{l|en|over}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈəʊvə/}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈoʊvɚ/}}

===Prefix===
{{en-prefix}}

# [[above]], or [[higher]]
#: {{m|en|overbar}}, {{m|en|overlook}}
# [[superior]]
#: {{m|en|overlord}}
# [[excessive]]ly
#: {{m|en|overkind}}, {{m|en|overloud}}, {{m|en|overstate}}
# [[surrounding]] or [[covering]]
#: {{m|en|overcoat}}, {{m|en|overpaint}}
# {{lb|en|augmentative}} [[intensely]], [[extremely]], or [[exceptional]]

====Usage notes====
Comparison of relative combinations (two separate words, hyphenated or a single compound word) does not easily fit a pattern; terms become compound words as they are broadly accepted.

